The conventional way to write multi-line JSX for clear separation and readability is to wrap it in parentheses. 

Examples of incorrect code for this rule include:
```jsx
function MyComponent() {
  return (
   <div>
     <p>Hello</p>
     <p>World</p>
   </div>
  )
}

```

The correct way to format multi-line JSX is to wrap it in parentheses for improved readability:
```jsx
function MyComponent() {
  return (
    <div>
      <p>Hello</p>
      <p>World</p>
    </div>
  );
}
```
Additionally, it's a good practice to use camelCase to name attributes.

